course: dictionary
lesson: 4869
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word icon can mean a small picture on a screen, a holy painting in a church, or a very famous person. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, which are its context. «Click the icon to open the app» tells you it is a picture on a screen, because you click it.
explain: Look for clues in brackets and in the words that describe it. «The Orthodox Church is known for icons (painted holy pictures of Jesus and the saints, which people kiss)» tells you the icon is a painting, because the brackets explain what it is. Holy pictures of saints are found in churches, not on phones.
explain: Check the clues with the word «tiny». «A good logo is simple enough to recognise on a giant poster and on a tiny phone icon» shows that an icon can be small enough to fit on a phone. Swap in your meaning and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have chosen well.
fact: Icon means a small picture on a computer, tablet or phone screen that you click or tap to open an app.
fact: In churches, an icon is a holy painting of Jesus, Mary or a saint, often used to help prayer.
fact: An icon can also be a very famous person or thing that stands for an idea, such as «a fashion icon».
fact: Orthodox Christians often use icons in worship, but some Christians do not use them, so the point is debated.
fact: When a word has more than one meaning, the context tells you which meaning the writer means.
exercise: «Click the icon to open the app.» What is an icon in this sentence? | A holy painting in a church | A famous singer | *A small picture on a screen that you tap to open an app
exercise: «The Orthodox Church is known for icons, painted holy pictures of Jesus and the saints, which people kiss.» What does icon mean here? | A painting of Jesus or a saint | *A holy painting | A famous person in pop music | A tiny button on a phone
exercise: «She is a fashion icon.» What does icon mean? | A small picture on a screen | A painting of a saint | A type of church | *A very famous person who stands for an idea
test: «Pray before the icon, then light a candle.» What does icon mean in this sentence? | A holy painting of Jesus or a saint | *A holy painting of Jesus or a saint used to help prayer | A small picture on a screen | A famous singer who is loved by many
test: «The logo is simple enough to recognise on a giant poster and on a tiny phone icon.» What is a phone icon? | A large painting | *A tiny picture on a phone screen you tap | A famous person on television | A holy picture of a saint
exam: Ella reads, «The national icon stood proudly on the hill.» Which meaning fits best? | A tiny button on a tablet | *A very famous thing that stands for a country | A small picture you tap on a screen | A holy painting in a church
